  "abstract": {
    "value": "An alternative strategy to overcome yield limitations in enzyme-catalyzed transformations is to use prochiral substrates. Thus, by selective transformation of one out of two enantiotopic groups, elements of symmetry are eliminated and optically active products can be obtained in high yield.<sup>[10]</sup> Herein, we report on our investigations regarding a novel protocol for the lipase-catalyzed desymmetrization of prochiral allenic diols through selective transesterification,<sup>[11]</sup> which yields highly enantioenriched axially chiral monoesters (Scheme 1, bottom).",
